# Schedule for the elf-sysv-nt build worker.
#
# Copy this to etc/CRONTAB, edit the two assignments below, and install it with
# `crontab etc/CRONTAB`. The live copy is ignored by git, because its paths are
# true of one machine and nobody else's checkout wants them.
#
# Cron hands each command to /bin/sh with the assignments in this file already
# in the environment, so $REPO expands in the lines below. That is the whole
# reason the machine-specific part is two lines at the top and nothing further
# down: change these, change nothing else.

REPO=/path/to/elf-sysv-nt
HOME=/home/you

# One tick of the headless worker. It takes the lock, builds the next
# dependency-ready package, and exits; a tick that finds the lock held does
# nothing and costs nothing. Five minutes is short enough that a killed tick
# loses little and long enough that two ticks do not overlap on a slow build.
*/5 * * * * $REPO/bin/elf-build-worker --model opus --effort medium

# The full nightly, commented out because it is not the default posture. It
# rebuilds rather than increments, so it wants a window with nothing else
# holding the toolchain, and it will fight the five-minute worker above if both
# run. Pick one.
# 0 3 * * * $REPO/bin/nightly-full >/dev/null 2>&1
